hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22880","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Mukhariq, from his father, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: What do you think, if a man comes wanting to rob me or take from me, what do you command me with? He said: You adjure him by Allah. He said: So if I do and he does not desist? He said: You seek help from the ruler. He said: So if there is no one of them near me? He said: You strive against him, or you fight him, until you are recorded among the martyrs of the Hereafter, or you protect your wealth."
"22881","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabus ibn Mukhariq, from his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet and said: What do you think, if a man comes to me taking my wealth? He said: You remind him of Allah, exalted. He said: What do you think, if I remind him of Allah? He said: So if I do and he does not desist? He said: You seek help against him from the ruler. He said: What do you think, if the ruler is far from me? He said: You seek help from the Muslims. He said: What do you think, if none of the Muslims is present with me and he hastens upon me? He said: So fight until you secure your wealth or are killed, so you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter."
